            "review_text": "digitalroc\nCalgary, Canada2299 contributions\n0\nA club of variety\nDec 2019\nWe came here from another bar across the street, and to tell you the truth, not sure why anyone would order food here, this is more of a club vibe, than a pub. The music was great, but the first floor was packed, no tables and a bit pushy, so we ventured up to the third floor. This was more tamed, the ability to view the chaotic street of Bui Vien and have a drink with the group. \n\nWe soon discovered that we were able to control the music on this floor, so we ended up queuing a bunch of songs up which made for a great night of fun! I don’t remember the price of bottled beers, but average for the bar scene, and worthy to mention was the service was good on this floor of the bar.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten January 26, 2020",
